      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like this removes the refusal that aosp/4368077 added here, so that 4KB processes can map the ring buffer.\n\nThe mapping itself looks right to me: with a 16KB-aligned offset, `vm_insert_pages()` maps the slices of each page by address since aosp/4368056, and user space finds the sub-buffers through `meta_page_size`, as `Documentation/trace/ring-buffer-map.rst` and `map_test.c` do.\n\nWould it be OK to keep the refusal, though, as I asked for BPF maps on aosp/4367949 and aosp/4367950? I may be missing a user: as far as I know, the tracefs readers on Android (Perfetto\u0027s traced_probes, atrace) are native processes, and apps can only write `trace_marker`. 4KB processes would still be able to `read()` and `splice()` `trace_pipe_raw`, and this patch wouldn\u0027t be needed.\n\nIf a 4KB process does need the mapping, could the commit message name it and say that this removes the refusal from aosp/4368077? `trace_ring_buffer_mmap_p3s.c` from aosp/4367986 could then move into this patch too.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "c398ed1d41238acff0747d7d8f556537344ee1f6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
